==English==
[[File:Magnificent CME Erupts on the Sun - August 31.jpg|right|thumb|a '''filament''' of solar material]]
[[File:Carbonfilament.jpg|right|thumb|a glowing light bulb '''filament''']]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|filamentum|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|filare||lang=la|to spin, draw out in a long line}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|filum||lang=la|thread}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[fine]] [[thread]] or [[wire]].
# Such a wire, heated to [[glowing]], in an [[incandescent]] [[light bulb]] or a [[thermionic valve]].
# {{botany}} The stalk of a [[stamen]] in a [[flower]], supporting the [[anther]].
# {{textiles}} A [[continuous]] [[object]], limited in [[length]] only by its [[spool]], and not cut to length.

